====Seats in doubt====
{{As of|2019|5|31}}, the AEC lists two divisions as "close seats" with a two-candidate margin of less than 0.5 percentage points: [[Division of Bass|Bass]] TAS (Liberal ahead), and [[Division of Macquarie|Macquarie]] NSW (Labor ahead).<ref name="closeseats">{{cite web |title=Close Seats |url=https://tallyroom.aec.gov.au/HouseCloseSeats-24310.htm |website=AEC Tally Room |publisher=Australian Electoral Commission |accessdate=21 May 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190518100652/https://tallyroom.aec.gov.au/HouseCloseSeats-24310.htm |archive-date=18 May 2019 |dead-url=no }}</ref>

The ABC lists only Macquarie as being "in doubt".<ref name="abcindoubt">{{cite web |title=Seats in doubt |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/elections/federal/2019/results/list?filter=indoubt&sort=az&state=all |website=ABC Elections |publisher=Australian Broadcasting Corporation |accessdate=21 May 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190521003316/https://www.abc.net.au/news/elections/federal/2019/results/list?filter=indoubt&sort=az&state=all |archive-date=21 May 2019 |dead-url=no }}</ref>

